501:
The prohibitions of this division shall not apply to:
(1) Any noise or sound made for the purpose of alerting persons to the existence of an emergency or any noise or sound that is made in the performance of emergency work;
(2) Any noise or sound emanating from any school activity or event or any organized athletic activity or event, including but not limited to any game, match, practice and performance;
(3) Any noise or sound made by law enforcement personnel or a public employee in the performance of a public function or duty;
(4) Any noise or sound made by domestic animals;
(5) Any noise or sound made by a burglar or vehicle alarm;
(6) Any noise or sound made by any religious worship activity, chime or bell produced from or by a church or other house of worship;
(7) Any noise or sound emanating from any activity, concert, event, festival or performance as may be permitted by the governing authority or its designee;
(8) Any noise or sound produced by radio, tape player, or other mechanical noise or sound making device or instrument from within a motor vehicle on a street or highway, which noise or sound is controlled by the O.C.G.A. § 40-6-14, as amended;
(9) Any noise or sound created or produced in connection with any government construction, demolition or maintenance project or any utility company construction, demolition or maintenance project;
(10) Any noise or sound emitted by a lawn mower, edger, trimmer, blower, power-driven hedge shear, and other lawn maintenance equipment when such noise or sound occurs on any day between the hours of 6:00 a.m. and 10:00 p.m.;
(11) Any noise or sound emitting by any watercraft upon any watercourse, lake, pond, creek, river, or swamp when operated in accordance with applicable Georgia laws; and
(12) Any noise or sound emitted by any machinery used in the ordinary course of a commercial or industrial business on any day between the hours of 6:00 a.m. and 10:00 p.m.
(Ord. No. 2022-2, § I, 4-4-2022; Ord. No. 2022-5, § I, 7-11-2022)
